## 3. Conclusion
In summary, we propose a new synthetic strategy to obtain large-area \( (2400\;\mathrm{cm}^{2}) \) ultrathin \( (210{-}300\;\mathrm{nm}) \) and rollable MOF membranes via a step-nucleation in situ self-repair approach. The mixed metal-ion/ZIF membranes having a large area and low
selective-layer thickness are normally difficult to obtain. Our synthetic strategy led to the successful preparation of different ZIF membranes. The large-area ultrathin and rollable ZIF-8 and mixed metal-ion/ZIF membranes display ultrahigh gas permeance and good mixed-gas selectivity. Good mixed-gas selectivity signifies that the ZIF-8 surface covering of the flexible polymeric membrane support is complete and is fit for purpose, while not implying that the ZIF-8 crystal structure is defect-free, since there are intentional open metal-ion sites. These membranes were used to prepare spiral-wound membrane modules, which show enhanced gas separation performance compared with current membrane modules. The membrane area within the module was \(\approx 4800~\mathrm{cm}^{2}\), which is over one to two orders of magnitude greater than the area of current ZIF membrane modules. This work provides a promising strategy to fabricate large-area ultrathin and rollable ZIF membranes on polymer supports, which would greatly promote the practical applications of ZIF membranes.
## 4. Experimental Section
All the reagents were of analytical grade and used as received. Cobalt nitrate hexahydrate \(\left(\mathsf{C o}(\mathsf{N O}_{3})_{2}{\cdot}6\mathsf{H}_{2}\mathsf{O}\right)\), zinc nitrate hexahydrate \(\left(\mathsf{Z n}(\mathsf{N O}_{3})_{2}{\cdot}6\mathsf{H}_{2}\mathsf{O}\right)\), copper nitrate trihydrate \(\left(\mathsf{C u}(\mathsf{N O}_{3})_{2}{\cdot}3\mathsf{H}_{2}\mathsf{O}\right)\), and 2-methylimidazole \((98\%)\) were obtained from Enokai Technology Co., Ltd. (China). 1,3,5-Benzenetricarboxylic acid \(\left(\mathsf{H}_{3}\mathsf{B T C}\right)\) was obtained from J&K Scientific Ltd. (China). PDMS, tetraethyl orthosilicate (TEOS), dibutyltin dilaurate (DBD), and PVA (degree of polymerization, 1700; degree of hydrolysis, \(87{-}89\%\) ) were purchased from Aladdin Reagent Co., Ltd. (China). Deionized water was obtained from a Hitech laboratory water purification system. N-Heptane, N, N-dimethylformamide (DMF), anhydrous methanol, and ethanol were obtained from Shanghai Macklin Biochemical Co., Ltd. (China), and used without further treatment. PSf ultrafiltration membranes (mean pore diameter, \(20{-}30\ \mathrm{nm}\)) were obtained from Shandong Jiuzhang Membrane Technology Co., Ltd. (China) and immersed in deionized water for \(12\,\mathrm{h}\) before use.
The Supporting Information contains details of the procedures used to prepare the ZIF-8, ZIF-67, and Cu-BTC nanoparticles, mPSf organic PDMS interface layer, and ZIF-8, ZIF-67, Cu-BTC, and mixed metal-ion/ZIF membranes; the experimental characterization techniques, including XPS, FTIR, XRD, SEM, AFM, pore structural analyses, and membrane gas separation performance test; and the experiments and theoretical simulations of the formation mechanism of the MOF membranes.
